# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# QTIServices frontend — backend configuration
#
# The Spring Boot backend lives at:
#     https://main.myonlineclasspro.com
#
# Pick ONE of the two modes below. Mode A is the default and is what you want
# unless you are running the frontend on a Node server on the same host.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── MODE A — Direct (browser calls the backend cross-origin) ─────────────────
# Works with any hosting, including static/Hostinger. Requires CORS on the
# backend (see the note at the bottom of this file).
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://main.myonlineclasspro.com

# ─── MODE B — Proxy (Next.js forwards same-origin paths to the backend) ───────
# Avoids CORS entirely because the browser only ever talks to your own origin.
# Requires a running Node server (`next start`) — rewrites do NOT work with a
# static export. To use it: blank out NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL above and set:
#
# BACKEND_ORIGIN=https://main.myonlineclasspro.com

# ─── WebSocket (chat) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Always point this at the backend directly. Next.js rewrites cannot proxy a
# WebSocket upgrade, so routing the socket through Mode B's proxy will fail even
# when the REST calls succeed.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=https://main.myonlineclasspro.com/ws/chat

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Backend requirements for MODE A
#
# Because the browser calls the backend from a different origin, Spring Boot
# must allow it. Auth is a Bearer token from localStorage — NOT a cookie — so
# allowCredentials is not required.
#
#   - Allowed origin:  your frontend origin (e.g. https://qtiservices.com)
#   - Allowed methods: GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, OPTIONS
#   - Allowed headers: Authorization, Content-Type
#   - The SockJS/STOMP endpoint (/ws/chat) needs the same origin allowed in its
#     own registry config — Spring's WebSocket CORS is configured separately
#     from the MVC one.
#
# NEVER put JWT signing secrets, DB credentials, AWS keys or Stripe secret keys
# in this file. Anything prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ is shipped to the browser.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
